<svelte:head><title>Simulation terms · OmieBot</title></svelte:head><main><a href="/invest">← Trading capital workspace</a><h1>Simulation terms</h1><p>Version simulation-v1 ·16 October2026</p><h2>No investment offer or real funding</h2><p>All credits are fictitious USD, have no monetary value, cannot be transferred and cannot be redeemed for money. No client money is held in escrow or traded. This simulation does not establish a live investment contract.</p><h2>Age and risk</h2><p>Adults18+ only. Trading can lose all invested capital. Targets, probabilities and simulated returns do not promise future returns or income. Do not rely on trading to pay essential expenses.</p><h2>Illustrated fees and redemptions</h2><p>The proposed fee is10% of the principal portion actually redeemable upon withdrawal. Deposits and gains are excluded from this fee basis. Losses reduce redemption value. Original principal is not guaranteed. The illustrative3–7 working-day window excludes weekends and is not a live payout promise.</p><h2>Live agreements remain subject to professional review</h2><p>Before a live offering, documents must identify the legal operator, registrations, permitted countries, independent custodian, asset segregation, execution mandate, valuation and unit pricing, profit/loss allocation, fees, conflicts, KYC/AML and sanctions rules, eligibility, privacy and international transfers, tax, complaints, redemption suspensions, insolvency, governing law and dispute resolution. Nigerian registration alone cannot establish global authorization.</p><h2>Simulation consent and records</h2><p>Allocation records retain acknowledgment of this version. Trading Pool means combined capital with stake-based profit and loss allocation. Trading Squad means two or more participants agreeing a trading term and distribution intervals. Single-Folder Trading means separately accounted individual capital. Pairing suggestions or requests require participant opt-in and approval. Current selections record simulation preferences only; no matching, pooling or money movement occurs. Authenticated records belong to the account and consume backend resources. No simulation acknowledgment substitutes for legally reviewed live documents.</p></main><style>main{max-width:800px;margin:50px auto;padding:24px;color:#dce4ee}h1{font-size:40px}h2{margin-top:32px;font-size:21px}p{color:#a6b2c2;line-height:1.9;font-size:14px}a{color:#e6b85c}</style>